NAME
  apt-ftparchive - generate repository index files

SYNOPSIS
  apt-ftparchive packages DIR
  apt-ftparchive release SUITEDIR

DESCRIPTION
  apt-ftparchive builds the index files that apt reads. It scans a
  directory of .fpkg archives and writes a Packages index, or scans a
  suite directory and writes its Release file. Output goes to stdout;
  redirect it into place.

  There is no signing and no compression. Release lists the SHA256 and
  size of every file below the suite directory so apt can verify the
  component indexes it downloads.

COMMANDS
  packages DIR
    Recursively find every *.fpkg under DIR, read each archive's control
    fields, and print one Packages stanza per archive. Each stanza
    carries the package's control fields plus:
      Filename:  path relative to the current working directory, using
                 forward slashes and no leading ./
      Size:      archive size in bytes
      SHA256:    archive SHA256
    Run it from the repository root so Filename is repository-relative:
      apt-ftparchive packages pool > dists/freax/main/binary-all/Packages
  release SUITEDIR
    Print a Release stanza for the suite. Components are the
    directories directly under SUITEDIR; the architecture is always all.
    Includes Suite, Codename, Date, Architectures, and Components, plus
    a SHA256 and Size line for every file recursively under SUITEDIR,
    excluding the Release file itself:
      apt-ftparchive release dists/freax > dists/freax/Release

REPOSITORY LAYOUT
  A repository produced with these tools looks like:
    dists/freax/Release
    dists/freax/main/binary-all/Packages
    pool/main/<package>_<version>_all.fpkg
  Place archives under pool/<component>/ and generate the index from the
  repository root so the Filename fields point at that location.

EXAMPLES
  apt-ftparchive packages pool > dists/freax/main/binary-all/Packages
    Build the main component index.

  apt-ftparchive release dists/freax > dists/freax/Release
    Build the release file for the freax suite.